#
FinOps Secure Audit Trails and Compliance Logs Documentation
#
When an application has the power to manage high-stakes corporate infrastructure, maintaining an unalterable log of user actions is required for compliance and forensics. This system ensures accountability by instantly streaming audit logs to a secure, external vault outside of the hosting server.
#
🏗️ 1. The Audit Log Architecture
The application uses a dual-logging strategy. Every time an optimization action occurs (such as resizing a server), the backend logs it in two places simultaneously:
#
                  ┌───────────────────────────────┐
                  │    FinOps Dashboard Action    │
                  └───────────────┬───────────────┘
                                  │
         ┌────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┐
         ▼                                                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│     Local Backup Logging        │       │    External Enterprise Vault    │
│  (backend/logs/destroy-audit)   │       │   (Azure Log Analytics/SIEM)    │
├─────────────────────────────────┤       ├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ • Fast local text stream file   │       │ • Sent via secure HTTPS webhook │
│ • Good for quick diagnostics    │       │ • Completely unalterable log    │
│ • Vulnerable if server crashes  │       │ • Permanent compliance history  │
└─────────────────────────────────┘       └─────────────────────────────────┘
#
🛠️ 2. How to Activate Secure Webhook Streaming
Your repository already includes code that looks for an external log sink. To activate it, you do not need to write new code—you just need to pass an endpoint URL into your environment variables.

#
Step A: Set Up Your Log Sink in Azure
1. Log into your Azure Portal.
2. Search for and open Log Analytics Workspaces or Azure Monitor.
3. Create a new workspace and generate a unique Data Collection Endpoint Webhook URL.

#
Step B: Inject the Secret into Render
1. Open your Render Dashboard and click on your Backend Web Service.
2. Go to Environment on the left menu.
3. Click Add Environment Variable and add this exact key:
4. AUDIT_WEBHOOK_URL: Paste your secure Azure Log Analytics webhook link here.
5. Click Save Changes.

As soon as the backend restarts, it will automatically begin streaming every user click, view, and resource adjustment straight to your permanent Azure log warehouse.
