4. Enable Azure Activity Logs at the Subscription Scope
Every billing-affecting action (resource creation, deletion, resizing, role assignment changes) is recorded in the Azure Activity Log. This must be enabled across the entire FinOps subscription.

#
PowerShell
# 1. Create a dedicated Log Analytics workspace to centralize audit data
az monitor log-analytics workspace create --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --workspace-name finops-audit-logs --location eastus

# 2. Stream the entire subscription's Activity Log into that workspace
az monitor diagnostic-settings create --resource "/subscriptions/<your-subscription-id>" --name "finops-activity-audit" --workspace "/subscriptions/<your-subscription-id>/resourceGroups/FinOps-Backend-RG/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/finops-audit-logs" --logs '[{"category":"Administrative","enabled":true}]'

#
What to Expect Next: Every Administrative event (e.g., "Update Role Assignment", "Delete Virtual Machine", "Resize Virtual Machine") now flows into the finops-audit-logs workspace within minutes.
#
5. Capture Cost Management Data Exports for Billing Compliance
For billing compliance (chargeback, showback, external audits), cost data must be exported on a schedule to durable storage. Azure Cost Management exports generate daily CSV files you can retain for years.

#
PowerShell
# 1. Create a container to hold immutable billing snapshots
az storage container create --name finops-cost-exports --account-name <storage-account>

# 2. Create a daily export of the current month's actual costs
az costmanagement export create --scope "/subscriptions/<your-subscription-id>" --name "daily-actual-cost-export" --export-type ActualCost --timeframe MonthToDate --storage-container finops-cost-exports --storage-account <storage-account> --recurrence Daily --schedule-from 2026-01-01 --schedule-to 2030-12-31
#
6. Enforce Immutable (Write-Once) Retention
Compliance logs are worthless if an attacker (or a careless engineer) can delete them. Apply policy-based immutability so archived billing snapshots cannot be modified or deleted for the required retention window.

#
PowerShell
# Enable versioning on the storage account (prerequisite for immutability)
az storage account blob-service-properties update --account-name <storage-account> --enable-versioning true

# Set a time-based retention policy on the export container (e.g., 5 years)
az storage container immutability-policy create --account-name <storage-account> --container-name finops-cost-exports --period 1825 --policy-mode Locked
#
7. Send Security-Relevant Events to Microsoft Sentinel
To detect suspicious FinOps activity (e.g., a role upgrade to Contributor, mass VM deletion), connect the audit workspace to Microsoft Sentinel and build analytics rules.

#
PowerShell
# Connect Sentinel to your Log Analytics workspace
az sentinel create --workspace-name finops-audit-logs --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --location eastus

# Confirm the connector is linked (list current data connectors)
az sentinel data-connector list --workspace-name finops-audit-logs --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG
#
Then create a scheduled query rule that alerts on high-risk role changes:
#
kusto
AzureActivity
| where OperationNameValue == "Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write"
| where Properties_d.responseBody.properties.roleName in ("Contributor", "Owner")
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, CallerIpAddress, SubscriptionId, CorrelationId
#
8. Route Function App Activity into the Same Archive
The serverless cost API (GetCloudCosts) must also leave an audit footprint. Forward the Function App's diagnostic logs to the same Log Analytics workspace so all layers share one timeline.

#
PowerShell
az monitor diagnostic-settings create --resource "<function-app-id>" --name "finops-function-audit" --workspace "/subscriptions/<your-subscription-id>/resourceGroups/FinOps-Backend-RG/providers/Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces/finops-audit-logs" --logs '[{"category":"FunctionAppLogs","enabled":true}]'
#
9. Query the Unified Audit Trail
Use Log Analytics to answer the three standard auditor questions: who, what, when.

#
kusto
// Who changed cost-related permissions?
AzureActivity
| where OperationNameValue contains "roleAssignments"
| summarize Changes = count() by Caller, CallerIpAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 1d)

// What billing actions occurred on a given day?
AzureActivity
| where TimeGenerated between (datetime("2026-01-01") .. datetime("2026-01-02"))
| where OperationNameValue contains "Microsoft.Compute" or OperationNameValue contains "Microsoft.CostManagement"
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, OperationNameValue, ResourceId

// When was the Function App invoked and did it succeed?
FunctionAppLogs
| where FunctionName == "GetCloudCosts"
| summarize Invocations = count(), Failures = countif(Level == "Error") by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
#
10. Retention and Archival Policy
Standard retention schedule for a FinOps compliance program:
1. Activity Logs (workspace): 365 days.
2. Cost Export CSVs (immutable container): 5 years.
3. Sentinel analytic rules/alerts: 90 days in workspace, archive after.
4. Immutable backup copy: Store a second copy in a different Azure region for disaster recovery.

#
Common Error: Diagnostic Settings Not Applying
If the Activity Log stops streaming, re-run the diagnostic settings create command with --export-to-resource-specific false. Some log categories do not support the resource-specific destination table.
